  "mechanismSummary": "Bu₃Sn• abstracts bromine from 6-bromohex-1-ene, giving the hex-5-enyl radical. Before it meets the dilute Bu₃SnH, the radical adds to its own alkene. It closes the five-membered ring (5-exo-trig) about 50 times faster than the six-membered one (6-endo), because only the near alkene carbon can be reached along the preferred line of attack. The cyclopentylmethyl radical takes H from Bu₃SnH: methylcyclopentane, with about 2% cyclohexane. Keeping Bu₃SnH dilute stops the uncyclised radical being reduced to hex-1-ene.",
